# LeakSanitizer suppressions, used by the debug, app and fuzz presets through LSAN_OPTIONS.
#
# Only leaks in code we do not own belong here (a driver, Qt, a system library), one line each
# with the reason above it, in the form `leak:<function, library or file name>`. A leak in our
# own code is fixed, never suppressed.

# Nothing from the Vulkan drivers is listed. Mesa's drivers (lavapipe, RADV) allocate state once
# per process and keep it in their own static data; when the Vulkan loader unloads a driver at
# vkDestroyInstance, LeakSanitizer reports that memory, from frames that have lost their names,
# so no entry could match the driver without also matching our own code. Instead these presets'
# test environment (CMakePresets.json) sets VK_LOADER_DISABLE_DYNAMIC_LIBRARY_UNLOADING=1, which
# keeps drivers loaded and the memory reachable: with it, lavapipe and RADV (Mesa 26.2) report
# nothing.
